Note: Gat 2: second, radically new approach to GAT task
Note: A and B gone from driver; C in driver
Note: GAT FTLD Task
Note: Distractor Condition: Frontal subject: Attention  = 1
Note: Assume that Semantic Distractors share some predicate semantic units with

Parameters
  Attention 0.1
  HebbLearningRate 0.9
  SaveGroupHebbs False
  SavePropHebbs False
  SaveSPHebbs False
Done

Analog Problem
  DefPreds
    Right 2 r1 r2 r3 r4 r5 r6 ; { the "right" relation: that between A and B
    WrongS 2 r1 r2 r3 w1 w2 w3 ; { a "wrong" semantic relation (another 'tween C and y)
    LookOf 1 l1 l2 l3 l4 l5 l6 ; { what C looks like
  end { defpreds
  DefObjs
    C c1 c2 c3 c4 c5 c6 c7 ; { this is the critical object
    X x ; { empty filler, x, of missing relational role in A:B::C:x
  end { defobjs
  DefProps
    P1 Right ( C X ) 200 ; { the "right" relation: that between A and B
    P2 WrongS ( C X ) 5 ;  { a "wrong" relation between C and some X
    P3 LookOf ( C ) ;
  end { defprops
Done { analog 0

Analog Alternatives?
  DefPreds
    Right 2 r1 r2 r3 r4 r5 r6 ; { shares 1 - 8
    WrongS 2 r1 r2 r3 w1 w2 w3 ;
    LookOf 1 l1 l2 l3 l4 l5 l6 ;
    OtherWrong 2 r1 l1 w1 o1 o2 o3 ;
  end { defpreds
  DefObjs
    Y y ; { call it Y rather than X to aviod semantic overlap
    Z z ;
    D d1 d2 d3 d4 d5 d6 d7 ; { right choice: for now no semantic overlap w/ C: all carried by preds
    SemAssoc a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 ; { other (wrong) semantic associate
    SimShape ss1 ss2 ss3 ss4 ss5 ss6 ; { similar-looking obj
  end { defobjs
  DefProps
    P1 Right ( Y D ) ; { the correct choice
    P2 WrongS ( Y SemAssoc ) ; { the other semantic associate
    P3 LookOf ( SimShape ) ;
    P4 OtherWrong ( Y Z ) ;
  end { defpreds
Done { analog 1

Sequence
  Driver=[ 0 ] { set analog 0 to driver
  Recip=[ 1 ]
  Order=[ R ( 1 1 ) ]
Done.
